Z||000000||Formula||09-13-1999||07:20 PM||||<BR>I was driving down the street at 20 mph.  Let off the gas and heard a clu-clunk. next my temp , and voltage warning lights came on.  Looking at the engine I noticed that the water pump pulley had completly came off.  I now have the water pump off but can't find a pulley for it any where. Does anyone know what cars I can take them off of.  No luck at the local salvage yard. And will the 2m4s pulley work on a formula?||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||09-13-1999||11:01 PM||||If you are asking if any 4 cyl fiero water pump pully will fit any other..... Yes.<P>Are there other cars that use the front side pully like fiero? I don't know. All the FWD 4cyls I've seen use the waterpump as an idler or "back side" pully. (I.E. it's flat just like the tensioner pully.<P>If you water pump pully came off.... I'd replace the pump. Could be that shaft is out of spec. ||||reg||5
